et in  Vermont I live in Vermont I know that  seems minor but they got a surprising  amount of things that just felt right  incorrect about Vermont in the way that  they he depicted all of it and I enjoyed  that before and I'm hoping to get more  of that again number three the happy  time murders this is another one that  I've been waiting for a long long time  for I remember first hearing about this  way back when they just couldn't get  funding for it and that has been a long  road so if you've never heard of the  happy  murders basically imagine Who Framed  Roger Rabbit  but instead of toons its puppets and so  it is an r-rated murder mystery in a  world that has both humans and puppets  and the puppets are kind of second-class  citizens and there's a puppet detective  and realize it is the Jim Henson company  making it this is not god this is not  gonna be like meet the Feebles where  it's kind of a cool novelty that is  puppets but you're left lying boy I wish  this was Muppet caliber puppetry going  on this is gonna be the Muppets  this is gonna be our rated Muppet level  puppetry and performance of the puppets  and that style of puppet I'm oh I'm so  excited about this I've been waiting on  this one for a long time and yes  number two Avengers infinity war it's  got a lot to live up to it's got a lot  going on it's got a lot of elements to  juggle it may not be possible for one  film to juggle this many characters and  this much build up and actually work but  damn I'm still excited to see it and I  still got chills on on the back of my  neck when I saw that first trailer and I  can't help but be excited everything in  my rational brain says dial back your  excitement keep it in check it's gonna  be almost impossible for this to live up  to the hype but my rational brain cannot  trump  my gut instinct which is just yeah I'm  super super pumped for this one it's  kind of impossible for me not to be  oddly though it's not my number one  movie that I'm most excited for although  the one I am is not far off the movie I  am most excited for going to 2018 is  Black Panther and it might seem odd to  some that I'm more excited for Black  Panther than infinity War part of that  has to do though with the fact that as  much as infinity war is going to deliver  bigger than I've probably ever seen from  a Marvel film it's also gonna be  bringing together a ton of elements that  I already know about and I mean I am  excited for that  but I get more excited about what's new  as opposed to giving me more of what I  already like just looking at the trail  for Black Panther getting a look at what  Conda getting a sense of this world in  these carriages and just getting a  feeling of I haven't seen this before I  love the aesthetic the afrofuturism look  and feel and vibe to the whole thing I'm  like this is really cool and for me and  what I have experienced in my lifetime  as in taker of entertainment this is  really new to me and it's exciting and  it's thrilling and it's in a genre I  love which is superheroes and it's a  character who I already know that I like  because I like chadwick boseman a lot  when he appeared in civil war but even  though I know him I don't know this  world he comes from I don't know these  other characters I am so excited to get  to know them and dig in and just find  out war and that is why Black Panther is  for me my most anticipated movie of 2018  so that's my list what are you most  excited for looking ahead to the next  year whatever it is drop something down  the comments let's talk about it like  subscribe follow me on Twitter at  Council of geeks give a listen to the  council geeks podcast Apple podcast and  stitcher radio I am one half of the  punch like a girl podcast that's a  presentation of the fire and water  podcast network Fire Water podcast comm  links for all the stuff is down below  and until next time as council is  adjourned  [Applause]  [Applause]

